<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms seek 22,500T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms seek 22,500T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd have jointly invited tenders to buy a total of 22,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat by 2:00 p.m. (0500 GMT) on Friday, traders said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Of the total, Cheiljedang has invited tenders for 7,000 tonnes at basis over May futures on the U.S grain futures exchanges, including the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour has invited the remaining 15,500 tonnes at flat prices.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for April 10-May 10 to the port of Pusan.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
